# What must NOT be uploaded when a function is deployed.
#
# `gcloud functions deploy --source=functions/<fn>` uploads that directory
# wholesale. Without this file it also ships the local tool caches: a deploy
# measured 23MB, of which 22MB was .mypy_cache and 216KB was the actual code.
#
# Two reasons this matters beyond upload time. A stale __pycache__ can shadow a
# source file that was deleted, so the deployed function runs code that is no
# longer in the repo. And tests carry fixtures — email templates, in this repo —
# which have no business on a production instance whatever they contain.
#
# gcloud reads this file the way git reads .gitignore, but does NOT fall back
# to .gitignore once this file exists, so anything that should be excluded has
# to be named here.

# Tool caches. Large, machine-local, and never needed at runtime.
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.mypy_cache/
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.venv/

# Tests and their fixtures. The function does not run them, and the fixtures
# are sample mail.
tests/
conftest.py
test_*.py
*_test.py

# Local configuration. Secrets reach a function through Secret Manager
# (see [tool.earthy] secrets in each pyproject.toml), never through a file in
# the bundle.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
creds.json

# Repo furniture that is not part of any function.
.git/
.gitignore
Makefile
README.md
*.md
uv.lock
tools/

# OS noise.
.DS_Store
